---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { fitTitle, fitDesc } from '../lib/seo';

const title = fitTitle(['Disclaimer: Reference Data, Not Trading Advice or Quotes']);
const description = fitDesc([
  'Why the exchange rates and commodity prices here are historical reference figures, not live quotes, forecasts, trading signals or personal financial advice.',
]);
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/disclaimer/" og="home"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Board', href: '/' }, { name: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer/' }]}>
  <div class="kicker">Disclaimer</div>
  <h1>Can you trade or make financial decisions from these figures?</h1>
  <p id="answer" class="lede">No. The figures are official reference data published once a day (ECB) or once a month (World Bank), shown for information and education. They are not live prices, not the rate a bank or broker will give you, not forecasts and not advice to buy or sell anything.</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Reference rates are not dealing rates</h2>
    <p>The ECB states that its euro reference rates are published for information purposes only and that using them for transaction purposes is strongly discouraged. Banks, card schemes and money-transfer services apply their own rates and fees. See <a href="/guides/ecb-reference-rates-explained/">ECB reference rates explained</a>.</p>
    <h2>Monthly averages are not spot prices</h2>
    <p>World Bank commodity prices are averages of a month’s benchmark prices. A physical buyer or futures trader on any given day could have paid much more or less. See <a href="/guides/world-bank-pink-sheet-explained/">what the Pink Sheet is</a>.</p>
    <h2>Statistics describe the past</h2>
    <p>Ranges, percentiles and volatility describe what has happened. They do not predict what will happen; past movements are not a reliable indicator of future results.</p>
    <h2>No personal advice</h2>
    <p>Nothing on the site takes your circumstances into account. Trading currencies, commodities and leveraged products carries a high risk of loss. Seek advice from a qualified, regulated professional before making financial decisions.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
